.SS custodian executor
.nf
usage: custodian executor [\-h] {start,approve,deny} ...

The delegated executor is a separate process that holds the only code path allowed to actually run a
governed skill script \-\- the calling agent's own process can only propose an action over a Unix
socket and never executes anything itself. An escalated action creates a signed, single\-use, digest\-
bound capability; approve it here, then resend the identical request to consume it.

positional arguments:
  {start,approve,deny}
    start               Start the executor process (blocks)
    approve             Approve a pending capability by id
    deny                Deny a pending capability

options:
  \-h, \-\-help            show this help message and exit
.fi
.SS custodian executor start
.nf
usage: custodian executor start [\-h] [\-\-skills\-root SKILLS_ROOT] [\-\-socket SOCKET]

options:
  \-h, \-\-help            show this help message and exit
  \-\-skills\-root SKILLS_ROOT
                        Skills directory (default: the bundled/dev skills root)
  \-\-socket SOCKET       Unix socket path (default: <state\-dir>/executor.sock)
.fi
.SS custodian executor approve
.nf
usage: custodian executor approve [\-h] \-\-approved\-by APPROVED_BY [\-\-digest DIGEST]
                                  [\-\-state\-dir STATE_DIR]
                                  capability_id

positional arguments:
  capability_id         Capability UUID, or 'latest'

options:
  \-h, \-\-help            show this help message and exit
  \-\-approved\-by APPROVED_BY
                        Operator identity for the audit trail
  \-\-digest DIGEST       Full action digest (64\-char hex) for verification before approval. If
                        provided and it does not match the capability, approval is rejected.
  \-\-state\-dir STATE_DIR
                        State directory (default: ~/.custodian or $CUSTODIAN_STATE_DIR)
.fi
.SS custodian executor deny
.nf
usage: custodian executor deny [\-h] [\-\-denied\-by DENIED_BY] [\-\-digest DIGEST]
                               [\-\-state\-dir STATE_DIR]
                               capability_id

positional arguments:
  capability_id         Capability UUID, or 'latest'

options:
  \-h, \-\-help            show this help message and exit
  \-\-denied\-by DENIED_BY
                        Operator identity (falls back to $USER)
  \-\-digest DIGEST       Full action digest (64\-char hex) to verify before denying.
  \-\-state\-dir STATE_DIR
                        State directory (default: ~/.custodian or $CUSTODIAN_STATE_DIR)
.fi
