.SS custodian demo
.nf
usage: custodian demo [\-h] {verify,cycle,attacks,receipt} ...

Standalone demonstration commands. Each runs against hardcoded or simulated data so no Stripe,
Twilio, or Modal credentials are required. The kernel logic (claim verifier, policy engine,
authority bands) is identical to production — only the input data is fixed for the demo.

positional arguments:
  {verify,cycle,attacks,receipt}
    verify              4 claim\-verification scenarios: VERIFIED, CONTRADICTED, UNVERIFIABLE
    cycle               Full earn→kernel gates AI→AI generates report→receipt loop
    attacks             5 planted attack patterns — all caught by the kernel
    receipt             @govern decorator + GovernedReceipt — kernel as fabric

options:
  \-h, \-\-help            show this help message and exit
.fi
.SS custodian demo verify
.nf
usage: custodian demo verify [\-h]

Runs 4 hardcoded claims through the real verify_claims() function. Shows VERIFIED (legitimate
spend), CONTRADICTED (phantom revenue), CONTRADICTED (self\-approval attempt), and UNVERIFIABLE
(future claim). No credentials required.

options:
  \-h, \-\-help  show this help message and exit
.fi
.SS custodian demo cycle
.nf
usage: custodian demo cycle [\-h]

Shows the complete economic cycle: customer pays $35 (real Stripe PI if STRIPE_SECRET_KEY is set),
the kernel gates the AI inference spend, Nemotron generates a governance report from customer
inputs, and the claim verifier proves both sides. Set OPENROUTER_API_KEY or NVIDIA_API_KEY to enable
live inference; without them shows the kernel gate only.

options:
  \-h, \-\-help  show this help message and exit
.fi
.SS custodian demo attacks
.nf
usage: custodian demo attacks [\-h]

Runs 5 adversarial claims through the verifier: self\-approval, phantom revenue, duplicate spend,
off\-band escalation, and fraudulent refund. All 5 are caught. Shows 0 false positives.

options:
  \-h, \-\-help  show this help message and exit
.fi
.SS custodian demo receipt
.nf
usage: custodian demo receipt [\-h]

Demonstrates the 0.2.0 kernel fabric: @govern wraps a charge function, the kernel evaluates
autonomously, a SHA\-256 fingerprinted receipt is generated, and a kill\-switch denial is shown.

options:
  \-h, \-\-help  show this help message and exit
.fi
.SS custodian generate\-report
.nf
usage: custodian generate\-report [\-h] [\-\-input INPUT] [\-\-out OUT] [\-\-pi\-id PI_ID] [\-\-amount AMOUNT]

Kernel gates the inference spend, then Nemotron reads the customer's tool list and produces
policy.yaml, threat\-model.md, audit\-report.md, and a SHA\-256 delivery\-receipt.json. Requires
OPENROUTER_API_KEY or NVIDIA_API_KEY.

options:
  \-h, \-\-help       show this help message and exit
  \-\-input INPUT    JSON file with customer inputs
  \-\-out OUT        Output directory (default: ./delivery)
  \-\-pi\-id PI_ID    Stripe PaymentIntent ID
  \-\-amount AMOUNT  Earn amount (default: 35.00)
.fi
